From f951ac7dc4e1a567be372e7f9b40af6b3d34f056 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:18:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Desktop: gateway-bound account recovery terminal
 with a fixed command

A panel that finds a dead Anthropic grant had no supported way to start the
sign-in for that exact stored row: core forbids a dashboard login for
Anthropic, and the only hand-off was Settings > Accounts, which shows CLI
instructions and would add a second row.

Add `window.hermesDesktop.terminal.startRecovery({connectionId, profile,
provider, credentialId})`. The caller names a gateway, a provider and a pool
row id and supplies no command text. Main checks each field against a fixed
pattern and runs only `hermes [--profile NAME] auth reauth PROVIDER ID`:
through this device's resolved Hermes runtime for the local gateway, or
through the gateway's recorded launcher over that gateway's SSH connection.

- A request that fails a check, a removed gateway, a gateway with no shell
  transport, a Windows host and an unknown remote launcher start no process
  and return `unavailable`; a gateway without a shell is never replaced by
  this device.
- The session is not a terminal tab (not listed, saved, restored or readable
  by agent terminal tools). Only the window that started it can attach, write,
  resize, read its cwd or dispose it. Ordinary shell tabs keep their existing
  write path.
- Only `anthropic` is accepted; Codex keeps the dashboard device sign-in.

Proof: electron/terminal-recovery.test.ts, 12 tests (argument checks, local and
SSH argv, every refusal, per-window ownership). They cannot run on the base
commit: the module and the IPC channel do not exist there. Existing terminal
IPC and external-terminal suites: 32 pass. "Open in terminal" now builds its
script from the same launcher helper (keeps main.ts within its line cap). tsc (renderer and electron projects) and eslint clean.
Not proven: a live Desktop run and a live Anthropic sign-in.
